course: dictionary
lesson: 12651
title: Disqualified: when the rules say no
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Disqualified means you are officially stopped from taking part in or winning something, because you broke a rule. The word is always linked to a rule, so look for the rule-breaking clue.
explain: «Tom started the race before the whistle, so he was disqualified.» The clue is started before the whistle. Tom broke a rule, so he cannot win. Try the swap check: "Tom was stopped from winning because he broke a rule." It still makes sense, so disqualified means stopped because of a rule.
explain: The same word is used outside sport too. «The driver was disqualified from driving for a year after the court's decision.» Here the rule is the law, and the driver is not allowed to drive. The clue from driving tells you what is not allowed.
explain: Look at the small words that come after it. We say disqualified from something, disqualified for something, or be disqualified. «The team was disqualified for cheating.» The word for, followed by a reason, tells you why.
fact: Disqualified is the past form of disqualify, so it describes someone who has already been stopped.
fact: «Disqualified» means officially stopped from taking part in or winning a competition because you broke a rule.
fact: In law, «disqualified» means not allowed to do something, such as drive or hold a job, because of a rule or a court decision.
fact: Common phrases are «disqualified from», «disqualified for», and «be disqualified».
fact: Context clues such as a broken rule, a court, or a reason after for help you work out what disqualified means.
exercise: «The swimmer touched the wall the wrong way and was disqualified.» What does disqualified mean here? | Allowed to swim again with no problem | Told to have a rest | Given a gold medal for being fast | *Officially stopped from winning because a rule was broken
exercise: «The judge said the runner was disqualified for starting too early.» Why was the runner disqualified? | *Because she broke the rule by starting too early | Because she was too tired | Because she ran the wrong way for fun | Because it was raining
exercise: «Ben was disqualified from driving after the court's decision.» What does disqualified mean here? | *Not allowed to drive, because of a court decision | Learning to drive at school | Allowed to drive any time he likes
test: Which word would fit best? «The swimmer was ___ for touching the wall the wrong way.» | Hungry | Luminous | *Disqualified | Ancient
test: What does «disqualified from driving» mean? | *Not allowed to drive, because of a rule | Driving in the rain | Learning to drive at school | Able to drive faster than everyone
exam: Read the clue. «Mia was disqualified from the spelling bee because she used a dictionary during the test.» What does disqualified show? | Mia won a prize for being clever | *Mia broke a rule and is officially stopped from winning | Mia was given extra time | Mia was too tired to spell
